-- title:
--   Places over a point bounded by double cosets
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $L$ a field extension of $K$, let $t \in L$, and assume $L$ is a finite Galois extension of the intermediate field $K\langle t\rangle = K(t)$ generated by $t$. Let $\Gamma_0$ be a group and $\sigma \colon \Gamma_0 \to \operatorname{Aut}_{K(t)}(L)$ a surjective group homomorphism, and let $\Gamma, K_{\mathrm{st}} \le \Gamma_0$ be subgroups with $\Gamma$ of finite index. Let $E$ be an intermediate field of $L/K(t)$ such that $\sigma(\gamma)$ fixes every element of $E$ pointwise for all $\gamma \in \Gamma$, let $c \in K$, and let $W$ be a place of $L$ over $K$ — that is, a valuation subring of $L$ containing the image of $K$, different from $L$ itself and a principal ideal ring — with $\operatorname{ord}_W(t - c) > 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_W$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Assume $W$ is stabilised by each $\sigma(k)$, $k \in K_{\mathrm{st}}$, acting through the semilinear automorphism $(\sigma(k), \mathrm{id}_K)$ of $L/K$. Finally let $x \in E$ be an element whose image in $L$ is $t$. Then the number of places $P$ of $E$ over $K$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P(x - c) > 0$ is at most the number of double cosets $\Gamma \backslash \Gamma_0 / K_{\mathrm{st}}$.
--
--   This is the upper-bound half of Hilbert's decomposition theory for the fibre of $E \to \mathbb{A}^1_K$, $x \mapsto c$: the places of $E$ above $t = c$ are parametrised by a quotient of $\Gamma_0$ on which the double cosets $\Gamma \gamma K_{\mathrm{st}}$ act trivially. It is applied in the study of fibres of the $j$-invariant map on modular curves, where $\Gamma_0$, $\Gamma$ and $K_{\mathrm{st}}$ are a modular group, a congruence subgroup and a cusp stabiliser.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_natCard_place_ord_sub_pos_le_natCard_doubleCoset.lean

